=== The Legend of Zelda ===
* The general gameplay is a reference to the original NES title, right down to the HUD. Coins, Keys, and Bombs are used similarly to Rupees, Keys, and Bombs in the NES game.
** The original flash version of The Binding of Isaac uses a HUD that is a nearly direct port of the original NES Zelda title's HUD.
* {{E|Pin}}, {{E|The Frail}}, {{E|Scolex}}, {{E|Needle}}, and {{E|Pasty}} may have all been inspired by Lanmola from The Legend of Zelda: A Link To The Past..
* {{E|Death's Head}} was likely inspired by Bubbles from The Legend of Zelda on the NES, as they are both skulls that are invulnerable and maneuver by bouncing off walls.
** {{E|Cursed Death's Head}} also has a similar cursing effect which prevents the player from attacking.
* {{e|Mom's Hand}} and {{e|Mom's Dead Hand}} are a reference to Wallmasters from The Legend of Zelda.
* {{I|Spirit Sword}} Behaves like the Master Sword in 2D Zelda games, but acts closest to how Link's sword acts in [[wikipedia:The Legend of Zelda: Link's Awakening|Link's Awakening]], which is also a reference to the [[Isaac's Awakening|challenge where it is obtained]].
* [[I AM ERROR]] - Reference to an NPC's dialogue in Zelda II: The Adventure of Link.
* {{E|Mother}} - The ability to deflect the Fistula attack is a reference to the Dead Man's Volley.
* Coop Babies #377 - #386 are refrences to characters from Legend of Zelda series: Link, Dark Link, Phantom, Octorok, Orange Moblin, Blue Moblin, Zelda, Zora, Tingle, Midna.
* Coop Baby #400 is a reference to Sheik.
* Coop Baby #426 is a reference to Darknut, while Coop Baby #427 is a reference to black Darknut.

