== Magic: The Gathering ==
* {{p|Chaos Card}} - Refers to [https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=603 Chaos Orb], which instructs the player to flip it onto the playing field and destroy any cards it touches when it lands, a behavior similar to how the in-game Chaos Card is thrown and instantly kills any enemy.
* {{i|Black Lotus}} - Refers to the [https://gatherer.wizards.com/pages/card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=600 Black Lotus], one of Magic: The Gathering's most powerful cards. The 3 hearts it adds to the player's health total are a play on how the lotus creates 3 mana of any color.[https://gatherer.wizards.com/pages/card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=600]
* {{i|Lord of the Pit}} - Refers to [https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=438662 Lord of the Pit], a creature that has flying similar to how the item gives Isaac flying.[https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=438662]
* {{i|Spirit of the Night}} - Refers to [https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=3315 Spirit of the Night], a creature that was popular in early Magic. Also has flying, similar to Lord of the Pit.
* {{i|Contract From Below}} - Refers to [https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=1147 Contract from Below], which allowed a player to add a card to the (now-defunct) ante in a match to draw cards.
* {{P|Huge Growth|dlc=a+}} - Refers to [https://scryfall.com/card/lea/197/giant-growth Giant Growth], which increases the power and toughness of the creature the card is used on. This effect is similar to the effect in game as the card increases Isaac's damage and size.
* {{P|Ancient Recall|dlc=a+}} - Refers to [https://scryfall.com/card/cei/48/ancestral-recall Ancestral Recall], which allows the player to draw three cards from their library. In game, the card works similarly by spawning three new card items.
* {{P|Era Walk|dlc=a+}} - Refers to [https://scryfall.com/card/vma/2/time-walk Time Walk], which allows the caster to take an extra turn, which is an incredibly powerful effect for the game. Isaac references this by granting the player the effects of both {{I|Stop Watch}} and {{I|Broken Watch}}; two time related items.
* {{i|Spindown Dice}} - Refers to [https://www.ebay.es/itm/192582576591 Spindown Dice], a dice using on Magic to count life.

== Dungeons & Dragons ==
The first released four main characters you could pick in D&D are some of the playable characters in BOIR, based on the health and abilities.
* {{C|Isaac}} - Fighter
* {{C|Magdalene}} - Cleric
* {{C|Cain}} - Thief
* {{C|Judas}} - Mage
* {{I|D4}}, {{i|The D6}}, {{I|D8}}, {{I|D10}}, {{I|D12}}, {{i|D20}} - The main/required 6 dice types used to play D&D.
* {{i|Monster Manual}} - Reference to the book series of the same name that is used to reference what monsters do what in the game.
* Dead God - Like {{i|Monster Manual}}, the achievement Dead God is a reference to the [[wikipedia:Dead Gods|Dead Gods]] adventure module for the second edition of [[wikipedia:Advanced Dungeons & Dragons]].

